# Changelog and releases

User-facing work **must** add a bullet under `CHANGELOG.md` **[Unreleased]** in the same change. Follow [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/) + [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/). Details: `CONTRIBUTING.md`.

```text
feat:   ### Features
fix:    ### Bug Fixes
perf:   ### Performance
docs:   ### Documentation
feat!:  ### Breaking Changes
```

Leave out `chore` / `test` / `style` unless a user would notice. Imperative voice (`- Add …`, `- Fix …`). Do not rewrite old version sections.

```bash
just release X.Y.Z                             # cut Unreleased, bump ao3kit + plugin
just release X.Y.Z publish                     # commit, push, zip, gh release
python makeplugin.py changelog                 # preview Unreleased
python makeplugin.py release X.Y.Z             # same as just release
python makeplugin.py release X.Y.Z --publish   # same as just release … publish
```

`--publish` uses [Unreleased] (now the versioned section) as the GitHub release body and attaches `wranglekit.zip`. Do not invent a second notes file. Fail the release if Unreleased has no bullets.

Every **0.x** release body must keep the pre-1.0 disclaimer (`calibre_dev.changelog.PRE_1_0_DISCLAIMER`): not rigorously tested, part-time OSS, prefer **Stable** (marked after the fact), try another release if one will not run. Do not strip it. Do not mark Stable at publish time.
